1
00:00:08,108 --> 00:00:09,700
Come on.

2
00:00:13,213 --> 00:00:15,738
- How much longer?
- I'm almost through.

3
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:22,554
Sh! Someone's coming. Guards.

4
00:00:27,994 --> 00:00:30,189
- The castle's waking up.
- Time to go. Now.

5
00:00:30,296 --> 00:00:33,663
We have to get the pact from the strongroom.
England's future depends on it.

6
00:00:33,733 --> 00:00:35,792
Robin. No time.

7
00:00:35,902 --> 00:00:37,597
Will.

8
00:00:39,005 --> 00:00:40,597
And quietly.

9
00:00:41,441 --> 00:00:43,170
Aaagh!

10
00:00:48,281 --> 00:00:50,146
There you go.

11
00:00:52,585 --> 00:00:54,348
- It's empty.
- Where's the pact?

12
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:55,854
Where's everything?

13
00:00:55,922 --> 00:00:58,891
I don't know, but what I do know
is it's a good job nobody's heard us.

14
00:00:58,958 --> 00:01:00,516
Last time there were dogs.

15
00:01:06,032 --> 00:01:07,659
Run?

16
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,054
You're not eating?

17
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:05,086
No.

18
00:02:05,925 --> 00:02:07,722
John, we have to go back and get that pact.

19
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:12,963
It's proof of treason. We show that
to the King and the Sheriff's history.

20
00:02:13,032 --> 00:02:14,932
Robin, we've no idea where it's hidden.

21
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,335
The alarm.

22
00:02:40,193 --> 00:02:42,252
Who said money doesn't grow on trees?

23
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:48,157
- Oh!
- Whoa! Oi!

24
00:02:49,202 --> 00:02:52,137
- I've no more than ten shillings.
- Here we go.

25
00:02:52,205 --> 00:02:55,538
- Then why resist?
- If you tell the truth, we'll only take a tenth.

26
00:02:55,608 --> 00:02:57,371
- Lie...
- And we'll take it all.

27
00:02:57,443 --> 00:02:59,536
- It's the truth.
- Then why not show us?

28
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:05,147
- I need every penny for the woman I love.
- You're going to buy a woman?

29
00:03:05,218 --> 00:03:06,913
To marry her.

30
00:03:08,188 --> 00:03:10,486
Her father borrowed money from Canon Birkley.

31
00:03:10,557 --> 00:03:13,117
- Yeah, we know Birkley.
- Yeah, wherever Birkley goes,

32
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:15,093
the Sheriff's not far behind.

33
00:03:15,161 --> 00:03:17,254
Her father signed a bond of debt.

34
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:20,390
- And now he can't pay?
- Not easily, no. He's dead.

35
00:03:22,001 --> 00:03:25,164
Oh, please. You're not going to believe this?

36
00:03:26,506 --> 00:03:29,339
The bond is locked away in the castle.

37
00:03:29,409 --> 00:03:33,004
And Beatrice remains in service to the Canon
until her father's debts are paid,

38
00:03:33,112 --> 00:03:35,774
- so I need every shilling.
- How much is the debt?

39
00:03:36,916 --> 00:03:38,884
£2,000.

40
00:03:38,952 --> 00:03:42,046
- Ten shillings won't get you very far.
- I'll pay what I can.

41
00:03:43,122 --> 00:03:46,580
- I'll keep paying until Beatrice is free.
- This gets better and better.

42
00:03:50,697 --> 00:03:53,791
- If your story is true, my friend...
- It is true.

43
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,596
- Course it isn't true.
- If your story is true,

44
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:59,262
if you really do have only ten shillings,

45
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:04,006
- then we will pay off your debt.
- What?

46
00:04:04,110 --> 00:04:06,101
- What happens if it is true?
- It isn't!

47
00:04:11,217 --> 00:04:14,516
You see, I told you. Ten shillings.

48
00:04:18,891 --> 00:04:21,086
What are you doing? That's all our money.

49
00:04:21,894 --> 00:04:24,192
So we're robbing from
the rich to give to the...

50
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:25,855
- Rich.
- Right.

51
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:29,732
It's to help him marry his sweetheart, Will.
Think of it as a wedding present.

52
00:04:29,802 --> 00:04:32,498
What?
- Can't we just give him a toasting fork?

53
00:04:32,572 --> 00:04:35,735
- We'll be broke.
- Go and fill the bottom of the chest with sand.

54
00:04:36,342 --> 00:04:38,810
We follow that money, we find the pact.

55
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:42,707
Look, trust me. I have a plan.

56
00:04:48,554 --> 00:04:52,354
Robin's favorite, this one.
Leads from outside straight into the castle.

57
00:04:52,425 --> 00:04:55,451
You know, a simple iron grille
in there would fix that.

58
00:04:56,496 --> 00:04:58,259
Mm.

59
00:04:59,165 --> 00:05:02,191
Bars on there.
Upgrade this young man to leather.

60
00:05:03,169 --> 00:05:05,137
He's a hero.

61
00:05:06,406 --> 00:05:10,001
That idea's almost as good
as emptying the strongroom.

62
00:05:11,811 --> 00:05:13,938
- What are you doing?
- I'm not doing anything.

63
00:05:14,013 --> 00:05:15,810
You're giving away all Robin's secrets.

64
00:05:16,716 --> 00:05:18,877
You advised the Sheriff about the strongroom.

65
00:05:18,951 --> 00:05:22,045
- Look, I'm fighting for my life here, Marian.
- Yes, you are.

66
00:05:22,755 --> 00:05:24,689
Stop now

67
00:05:24,757 --> 00:05:27,089
or I swear I will kill you.

68
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:33,325
- Something wrong?
- No.

69
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:35,799
- No.
- Just, er, meeting the locals.

70
00:05:36,769 --> 00:05:38,464
In.

71
00:05:40,807 --> 00:05:45,335
John of York, my dear son.
How wonderful to see you.

72
00:05:45,411 --> 00:05:48,209
- How much are you paying me this week?
- The lot.

73
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:51,783
My porters have the money to pay the bond.

74
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:53,478
I'm here to claim my bride.

75
00:05:54,554 --> 00:05:57,955
Oh, good. Well, the Sheriff
will be, er, delighted.

76
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,356
Have your men give it to the guards.

77
00:06:00,426 --> 00:06:03,361
You wait through there
and I'll give the Sheriff the good news.

78
00:06:11,738 --> 00:06:15,003
- I hope you know what you're doing, Robin.
- Trust me, John.

79
00:06:34,494 --> 00:06:36,689
- My lord.
- What?

80
00:06:36,763 --> 00:06:39,061
We have a problem. Please.

81
00:06:42,135 --> 00:06:44,729
I'm not being funny
but it doesn't look like a problem.

82
00:06:44,804 --> 00:06:46,772
It's the repayment of a loan.

83
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:51,400
- So what's the problem?
- It's the bond on the girl Beatrice.

84
00:06:51,511 --> 00:06:53,945
- York is waiting outside.
- York? It's too late.

85
00:06:54,013 --> 00:06:56,004
We've agreed to sell her to Durham. Anyway,

86
00:06:56,115 --> 00:06:59,209
you told me he had nothing.
Where did he get this money from?

87
00:06:59,318 --> 00:07:02,481
My lord, I couldn't say but it's all there.
The interest, everything.

88
00:07:02,555 --> 00:07:05,388
- What do I tell him?
- Use your initiative. Hm?

89
00:07:05,491 --> 00:07:08,119
- Tell him it was an act of God.
- My lord.

90
00:07:19,205 --> 00:07:21,571
- John.
- Beatrice.

91
00:07:23,042 --> 00:07:25,738
- What are you doing here?
- I'm here to save you.

92
00:07:25,812 --> 00:07:28,372
I've paid off the bond. We're to be together.

93
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:30,211
Come round.

94
00:07:34,253 --> 00:07:36,687
- Take her.
- What are they doing? What's going on?

95
00:07:36,756 --> 00:07:38,849
- You leave her alone!
- John!

96
00:07:38,925 --> 00:07:41,359
- What are you doing?
- The money. It's not all there.

97
00:07:41,427 --> 00:07:43,861
It is there. Every penny.
All the capital, the interest.

98
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:47,127
- Not the early redemption charges.
- The early... What?

99
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,599
It's another 500.

100
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:52,195
500.

101
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:55,797
- I'll marry her without the bond.
- Do you not understand how debt works?

102
00:07:55,908 --> 00:07:58,308
While I have the bond,
she is church property.

103
00:08:06,619 --> 00:08:08,746
I know where he got this from.

104
00:08:08,821 --> 00:08:10,846
- These boxes belong to Robin.
- How do you know?

105
00:08:10,923 --> 00:08:13,483
Well, cos I ni... Cos I know.

106
00:08:13,559 --> 00:08:15,925
Why would Robin Hood give money to a knight?

107
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:19,954
Well, he wouldn't, unless, er...
he thought he could get it back.

108
00:08:22,134 --> 00:08:25,797
Well, let's disappoint him, shall we?

109
00:08:27,306 --> 00:08:29,706
We're going to put it
in your little birdcage.

110
00:08:29,775 --> 00:08:31,766
It's time for the unveiling.

111
00:08:32,845 --> 00:08:34,813
My lord, this cage, is it wise?

112
00:08:34,914 --> 00:08:38,873
- It was your man's idea. It's genius.
- All that money where everyone can see it.

113
00:08:38,951 --> 00:08:42,944
Where everyone can see if Robin Hood's
going to steal it. That is the point.

114
00:08:58,771 --> 00:09:02,764
Where are they going? They should have
gone left. They've gone right.

115
00:09:02,842 --> 00:09:05,106
- Right leads back outside.
- Robin.

116
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:14,379
- This is not good.
- Meant to be leading us to the pact.

117
00:09:14,453 --> 00:09:16,944
- We're back where we started.
- Sh.

118
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:20,520
What's that?

119
00:09:24,697 --> 00:09:26,289
People,

120
00:09:26,365 --> 00:09:29,266
my... dear people.

121
00:09:29,969 --> 00:09:31,869
We are gathered here today

122
00:09:31,938 --> 00:09:35,965
to witness the unveiling
of my marvelous birdcage.

123
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:42,472
- What are you doing?
- We're trying to find the pact.

124
00:09:42,548 --> 00:09:44,743
Nottingham's exchequer.

125
00:09:45,518 --> 00:09:47,679
Our community chest.

126
00:09:48,521 --> 00:09:52,287
There for all to see,
demonstrating once again,

127
00:09:52,358 --> 00:09:55,794
my commitment to open government.

128
00:09:55,895 --> 00:09:57,453
Hm?

129
00:09:59,098 --> 00:10:02,465
And this, this latest addition

130
00:10:02,535 --> 00:10:04,560
to our fund,

131
00:10:04,637 --> 00:10:06,730
I have been reliably informed,

132
00:10:07,373 --> 00:10:11,002
has come from the coffers
of Robin Hood himself.

133
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:12,873
Ooh.

134
00:10:13,946 --> 00:10:17,109
- There goes our money.
- Archers all around. Clever.

135
00:10:17,183 --> 00:10:20,516
If you happen to see... Robin Hood

136
00:10:20,586 --> 00:10:22,781
and he asks you, "Have you seen my money?"

137
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:28,519
You can say to him, "The answer,
my friend, is blowing in the wind. "

138
00:10:28,594 --> 00:10:31,188
It was Allan's idea.

139
00:10:32,531 --> 00:10:36,524
He's informed the Sheriff of all the ways
in and out of the castle.

140
00:10:36,602 --> 00:10:38,263
A good scheme, I think.

141
00:10:38,337 --> 00:10:41,272
They're sealing off the exits.
You have to get out now.

142
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:45,538
- But what if Allan tells them about you?
- He won't. I've silenced him.

143
00:10:48,748 --> 00:10:50,511
Stop!

144
00:10:52,551 --> 00:10:55,213
- That's my money.
- What's that man doing?

145
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:57,585
- I want my bride.
- Is he mad?

146
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:59,454
Yes. He's in love.

147
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:03,553
I've settled the debt
and you've got your money.

148
00:11:04,130 --> 00:11:07,065
You're the thieves. You and the Canon.

149
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:08,964
Not Robin Hood.

150
00:11:12,638 --> 00:11:14,469
- Hang him.
- What?

151
00:11:20,146 --> 00:11:23,946
- Come on, John.
- Grab a corner!

152
00:11:24,917 --> 00:11:26,680
John!

153
00:11:28,054 --> 00:11:29,988
Jump!

154
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:33,886
Jump!

155
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:38,455
Now!

156
00:11:41,834 --> 00:11:44,496
- Come on!
- Run!

157
00:11:46,439 --> 00:11:48,532
John! John.

158
00:11:49,709 --> 00:11:51,267
Come on!

159
00:12:06,125 --> 00:12:08,593
- We've lost all our money.
- And we don't have the pact.

160
00:12:08,694 --> 00:12:11,162
What were you playing at?
You could have got us killed.

161
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:13,721
- Did you tell him it was our money?
- No, of course not.

162
00:12:13,799 --> 00:12:15,664
The Canon told me it wasn't enough,

163
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:18,465
he says I have to pay
early redemption charges.

164
00:12:20,106 --> 00:12:23,906
You know what? We need to have
a little chat with this Canon.

165
00:12:23,976 --> 00:12:27,002
I hear he takes confession
from the tavern girls every lunchtime.

166
00:12:31,650 --> 00:12:34,210
- They got away.
- Surprise. Not.

167
00:12:34,787 --> 00:12:37,779
Hood always gets away
and I'm getting rather tired of it!

168
00:12:39,792 --> 00:12:41,919
This time

169
00:12:41,994 --> 00:12:43,859
we go to him.

170
00:12:45,998 --> 00:12:47,989
Look, like I said to Gis, I...

171
00:12:49,301 --> 00:12:51,326
I can't tell you where Robin lives.

172
00:12:55,541 --> 00:12:57,566
Whose side are you on, Allan?

173
00:12:59,145 --> 00:13:02,808
- Even if I did tell you, he might have moved.
- Well, we'll find out, won't we?

174
00:13:02,915 --> 00:13:04,746
I want him dead.

175
00:13:06,519 --> 00:13:09,352
Yeah, but if he hasn't moved on,
he'll have set loads of traps up.

176
00:13:09,421 --> 00:13:11,412
- It'd just be too dangerous.
- Yes.

177
00:13:11,524 --> 00:13:14,721
Well, don't you worry
about that, eh, dear boy.

178
00:13:16,195 --> 00:13:18,163
We'll send you in first.

179
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:37,710
- Marian.
- Father.

180
00:13:37,783 --> 00:13:39,410
Shh.

181
00:13:39,518 --> 00:13:41,748
Father, Robin is in trouble.

182
00:13:42,822 --> 00:13:44,881
Allan is leading Gisborne to the camp.

183
00:13:44,957 --> 00:13:47,755
I need to find a way to get out
of the castle and warn him

184
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:50,387
but the Sheriff has blocked every exit.

185
00:13:50,496 --> 00:13:51,929
I don't know what to do.

186
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:54,397
Marian, do you want to
end up in a cell like me?

187
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,991
No. But I must warn Robin.

188
00:13:57,102 --> 00:13:59,798
- Is he worthy of these risks you take for him?
- Yes.

189
00:14:01,106 --> 00:14:03,734
- He can't change anything.
- Yes, he can.

190
00:14:03,809 --> 00:14:06,972
He's going to get the traitors' pact
and show it to the King.

191
00:14:07,046 --> 00:14:09,014
The Sheriff's days are numbered.

192
00:14:09,114 --> 00:14:11,912
And does Robin know where it is, this pact?

193
00:14:12,751 --> 00:14:14,810
No.

194
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:18,949
- But he'll find it.
- The pair of you.

195
00:14:19,558 --> 00:14:21,549
- You're dreamers.
- Dreamers?

196
00:14:22,461 --> 00:14:24,861
- Because we are not weak like you?
- How dare you.

197
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:26,693
You caused all this.

198
00:14:26,765 --> 00:14:30,360
You allowed the Sheriff to walk in
and take your job and you did nothing.

199
00:14:30,436 --> 00:14:33,371
- That is not true.
- And you condemn Rob...

200
00:14:34,607 --> 00:14:36,905
You should be helping us.

201
00:14:37,509 --> 00:14:40,672
- I don't have time for this.
- Marian.

202
00:14:41,914 --> 00:14:43,609
I'm ashamed of you sometimes.

203
00:14:52,458 --> 00:14:54,221
Marian.

204
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:21,412
- What do you want?
- I'm here to take confession.

205
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:23,420
Oh. Very good.

206
00:15:24,590 --> 00:15:28,788
- Yours.
- I've paid off Beatrice's bond. Where is it?

207
00:15:29,862 --> 00:15:31,727
- I don't have it.
- Is it in the birdcage?

208
00:15:31,797 --> 00:15:34,561
It's not, is it?
It's too exposed up there for papers.

209
00:15:34,633 --> 00:15:35,964
Well, how would I know?

210
00:15:37,002 --> 00:15:39,869
You don't understand. It's not just
my friend here who needs to know

211
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:42,703
- where the Sheriff keeps his documents.
- As God is my friend,

212
00:15:42,775 --> 00:15:44,606
I swear I don't know where they are.

213
00:15:44,710 --> 00:15:46,905
And I swear to you

214
00:15:46,979 --> 00:15:51,416
that, if you don't tell us,
God won't be your friend,

215
00:15:51,517 --> 00:15:54,384
- he'll be your next-door neighbor.
- Whoa, whoa.

216
00:15:56,121 --> 00:16:00,080
If you promise not to hurt me,
I will tell you the truth.

217
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:03,485
I promise.

218
00:16:03,562 --> 00:16:07,760
Listen, I have no idea where the Sheriff
keeps his papers but it doesn't matter.

219
00:16:07,833 --> 00:16:10,996
- Somebody else has already repaid the bond.
- What?

220
00:16:11,103 --> 00:16:13,162
- Who?
- The Earl of Durham.

221
00:16:13,238 --> 00:16:15,365
He will marry Beatrice on Saturday.

222
00:16:15,441 --> 00:16:18,569
- The Sheriff's made a deal.
- Beatrice would never marry another man.

223
00:16:18,644 --> 00:16:20,874
- She loves me.
- That's why we haven't told her.

224
00:16:20,946 --> 00:16:22,937
- That is immoral.
- Oh, grow up!

225
00:16:23,015 --> 00:16:25,506
Money has a way of making things moral.

226
00:16:26,185 --> 00:16:29,313
And Durham is paying more
than you could ever dream of.

227
00:16:29,388 --> 00:16:31,549
After all, she's a very pretty girl.

228
00:16:32,858 --> 00:16:36,794
At-at! You made a promise
before God not to hurt me.

229
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:41,666
He did.

230
00:16:46,372 --> 00:16:48,101
Oh!

231
00:16:48,941 --> 00:16:50,806
- I didn't.
- Thank you.

232
00:16:52,644 --> 00:16:57,308
Gisborne's men, get on the back!
Come on. Get up there. Get up!

233
00:16:57,383 --> 00:16:59,374
- Guy, I need a favor.
- No.

234
00:16:59,451 --> 00:17:01,942
I must get to a physician.
My father is getting worse.

235
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:05,821
Marian, you know the rules
governing your house arrest.

236
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:09,517
But I would be with you
and then I would come straight back.

237
00:17:10,062 --> 00:17:11,620
Please.

238
00:17:15,634 --> 00:17:17,295
Get yourselves together.

239
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:19,360
- We've work to do.
- Why? What happened?

240
00:17:19,438 --> 00:17:21,770
The Sheriff's selling Beatrice
to the Earl of Durham.

241
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:24,775
- We have to get her out.
- How? Allan's blocked all our ways in.

242
00:17:24,843 --> 00:17:26,572
Yeah.

243
00:17:26,645 --> 00:17:28,772
Don't worry, we'll think
of something. Come on.

244
00:17:33,786 --> 00:17:37,688
- I am truly beholden to you all.
- It's what we do.

245
00:17:38,257 --> 00:17:40,350
You have no idea what she means to me.

246
00:17:40,426 --> 00:17:43,395
Let me guess. You can't sleep
for thinking of her,

247
00:17:45,364 --> 00:17:47,594
you can't turn a corner
without hoping she'll be there.

248
00:17:47,699 --> 00:17:49,564
You have those feelings?

249
00:17:50,169 --> 00:17:51,864
I'm just guessing.

250
00:18:02,347 --> 00:18:05,407
Thank you. Once again, I am in your debt.

251
00:18:06,552 --> 00:18:11,148
Marian, I'm not comfortable with the way
the Sheriff has treated your father. Or you.

252
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:15,082
Do you need me to wait
while you go into the physician's?

253
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,185
No. Don't let me keep you.

254
00:18:18,030 --> 00:18:20,021
Go straight back.

255
00:19:09,248 --> 00:19:11,216
Come on.

256
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:13,216
Robin!

257
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:15,548
- Yes, my love?
- Get me down!

258
00:19:15,621 --> 00:19:17,816
- You're in danger.
- But you look so good up there.

259
00:19:17,923 --> 00:19:20,517
- You will pay, Robin of Locksley.
- Honestly.

260
00:19:20,592 --> 00:19:22,992
You look gorgeous from any angle.

261
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:27,599
- Ooh.
- How do I look from that angle?

262
00:19:27,666 --> 00:19:30,726
Listen to me. I was wrong.
Allan is out of control.

263
00:19:30,802 --> 00:19:33,293
He's leading Gisborne and his men here now.

264
00:19:33,372 --> 00:19:35,169
Allan?

265
00:19:39,578 --> 00:19:41,603
You should stay here with us.

266
00:19:41,713 --> 00:19:43,613
I cannot live in the forest.

267
00:19:43,715 --> 00:19:47,412
- Why not?
- Because green doesn't suit me.

268
00:19:48,453 --> 00:19:51,980
- It's your father, isn't it?
- I cannot turn my back on him.

269
00:19:53,125 --> 00:19:55,719
And I cannot be found here.

270
00:19:56,929 --> 00:19:59,625
- What I said before...
- What?

271
00:19:59,731 --> 00:20:02,029
You know.

272
00:20:02,634 --> 00:20:04,864
I said you were gorgeous.

273
00:20:06,104 --> 00:20:07,867
I meant it.

274
00:20:11,977 --> 00:20:13,808
And I meant what I said.

275
00:20:15,914 --> 00:20:18,178
One day you will pay, Robin of Locksley.

276
00:20:29,761 --> 00:20:32,389
Just guessing? Liar.

277
00:20:35,867 --> 00:20:38,495
We've closed up the camp.

278
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:42,373
Let's meet Gisborne and Allan
on the low road,

279
00:20:42,441 --> 00:20:45,001
give Allan the welcome he deserves.
This is war.

280
00:20:45,644 --> 00:20:47,339
Come on.

281
00:21:11,903 --> 00:21:13,871
Right, as the Sheriff said...

282
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:16,703
you take the lead.

283
00:21:18,143 --> 00:21:20,168
Well, we're not there yet.

284
00:21:21,647 --> 00:21:23,342
All right.

285
00:21:24,049 --> 00:21:25,949
Guards, wait there.

286
00:22:02,454 --> 00:22:04,513
I told you to hang back.

287
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:13,492
- Hood. I thought you said we weren't near?
- We're not.

288
00:22:14,399 --> 00:22:16,560
He knew we were coming.

289
00:22:22,407 --> 00:22:24,170
It's Robin!

290
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:39,180
Guy. Guy!

291
00:22:39,658 --> 00:22:41,421
Get on!

292
00:22:45,330 --> 00:22:46,991
They got away.

293
00:22:47,065 --> 00:22:50,626
Gisborne knows someone warned us.
He'll squeeze Allan to find out who it was.

294
00:22:50,736 --> 00:22:53,136
- Allan would not betray Marian.
- Yes, he would.

295
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:55,765
Allan is not betraying anyone.

296
00:22:56,808 --> 00:22:58,002
We're gonna see to that.

297
00:23:07,652 --> 00:23:09,586
Open up. Injured men here.

298
00:23:09,654 --> 00:23:11,952
Gisborne said you were all dead.

299
00:23:12,023 --> 00:23:14,355
Do we look dead? Open up!

300
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:35,375
Go to the tower, find the girl, get her out.

301
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:38,307
- And you?
- I'm gonna find Allan.

302
00:23:39,985 --> 00:23:41,748
Robin.

303
00:23:42,554 --> 00:23:44,078
Don't...

304
00:23:44,156 --> 00:23:46,021
Djaq,

305
00:23:47,526 --> 00:23:50,552
I know you liked him
but he has to be stopped.

306
00:23:51,163 --> 00:23:52,721
For all our sakes.

307
00:23:55,634 --> 00:23:58,501
- Good luck.
- Ready?

308
00:24:10,715 --> 00:24:12,546
- Robin.
- Expecting to find

309
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:14,710
your new friend Gisborne, Allan?

310
00:24:17,155 --> 00:24:20,181
Listen, I don't want you to get
the wrong idea. I had no choice.

311
00:24:21,660 --> 00:24:24,288
I would never take him to the camp.

312
00:24:24,362 --> 00:24:28,230
- I wouldn't. I love you, Robin, all of you.
- That's very touching.

313
00:24:30,602 --> 00:24:32,968
But, as they say...

314
00:24:33,038 --> 00:24:35,165
love hurts.

315
00:24:42,047 --> 00:24:43,810
Don't do it, Robin.

316
00:24:58,797 --> 00:25:00,492
- Let's just talk about this.
- Yeah.

317
00:25:00,565 --> 00:25:04,626
Let's talk. And you can start by telling me
where the Sheriff keeps his documents.

318
00:25:04,736 --> 00:25:07,967
I don't know. I just told him to empty
his strongroom, that's it.

319
00:25:08,039 --> 00:25:10,906
- You must know where he's moved the pact.
- I swear I don't.

320
00:25:13,144 --> 00:25:15,578
Maybe his room. There's a safe there.
Trust me, Robin.

321
00:25:15,647 --> 00:25:17,979
Trust you? No, I don't think so.

322
00:25:23,755 --> 00:25:26,383
- I told you I'd never betray you.
- You already have.

323
00:25:26,458 --> 00:25:28,426
And next you'll betray Marian.

324
00:25:30,662 --> 00:25:33,290
- I'm not a Judas.
- And I'm no Jesus.

325
00:25:38,236 --> 00:25:40,227
Marian?

326
00:25:40,338 --> 00:25:41,930
What happened to you?

327
00:25:42,007 --> 00:25:45,568
It's just... an incident in the woods.
It was nothing.

328
00:25:55,253 --> 00:25:56,811
How is Sir Edward?

329
00:25:56,922 --> 00:25:59,083
I was just on my way to see him, actually.

330
00:25:59,157 --> 00:26:01,091
I'll tell him you asked after him.

331
00:26:01,159 --> 00:26:03,093
That's kind.

332
00:26:05,030 --> 00:26:06,827
Marian...

333
00:26:09,935 --> 00:26:11,630
- there is another side to me.
- Guy.

334
00:26:14,272 --> 00:26:17,105
My father. I should like to visit him alone.

335
00:26:20,011 --> 00:26:21,774
Of course.

336
00:26:34,125 --> 00:26:35,820
Now...

337
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:39,226
Please. I don't wanna die.

338
00:26:39,331 --> 00:26:43,233
- That's the only way you're gonna escape me.
- Robin! Spare him.

339
00:26:45,170 --> 00:26:46,831
- I can't.
- Please.

340
00:26:46,938 --> 00:26:49,702
- Do it for me.
- Marian, I'm doing this for you.

341
00:26:50,308 --> 00:26:52,708
- To protect you.
- Robin. Robin, please.

342
00:26:53,345 --> 00:26:55,609
If you love me, you will let him go.

343
00:26:55,714 --> 00:26:59,377
I do love you. And that's why
I can't let him live.

344
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:02,147
Because one day he'll do something
to take you away from me.

345
00:27:02,220 --> 00:27:04,484
I wouldn't.

346
00:27:04,556 --> 00:27:07,923
Please. Don't taint us with his blood.

347
00:27:22,340 --> 00:27:26,401
You owe me your life.
Don't you ever betray me.

348
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:29,677
I won't.

349
00:27:40,925 --> 00:27:42,893
Took you a long time to tell me that.

350
00:27:45,163 --> 00:27:47,393
Tell you what?

351
00:27:47,465 --> 00:27:49,490
You know.

352
00:27:53,571 --> 00:27:55,732
I must have been half concussed.

353
00:27:56,641 --> 00:27:59,166
Well, you'll be fully concussed
if you don't watch out.

354
00:28:02,247 --> 00:28:04,181
I think I know where the pact is.

355
00:28:12,624 --> 00:28:14,819
Yes?

356
00:28:14,926 --> 00:28:17,622
We're here to escort the prisoner
to the Earl of Durham.

357
00:28:20,799 --> 00:28:23,165
Come along, my dear,
your future husband's waiting.

358
00:28:34,512 --> 00:28:36,275
Father?

359
00:28:37,415 --> 00:28:39,474
Father, I've brought you some food.

360
00:28:46,024 --> 00:28:48,219
I'm sorry about what I said.

361
00:31:00,358 --> 00:31:02,121
The pact.

362
00:31:19,210 --> 00:31:21,303
I knew it would be here.

363
00:31:36,527 --> 00:31:38,552
My keys.

364
00:31:39,931 --> 00:31:42,422
My keys. Guards! Guards!

365
00:31:42,533 --> 00:31:44,797
My keys. My keys. My keys were here.

366
00:31:55,346 --> 00:31:56,938
Sh.

367
00:32:08,426 --> 00:32:10,189
So...

368
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:12,923
what do we have here, huh?

369
00:32:13,831 --> 00:32:16,197
My old friend

370
00:32:16,267 --> 00:32:18,497
goody two-shoes.

371
00:32:18,569 --> 00:32:20,400
- Looking for me, Sheriff?
- Guards!

372
00:32:22,540 --> 00:32:24,303
After him!

373
00:32:24,842 --> 00:32:26,707
Get after him!

374
00:32:35,153 --> 00:32:36,814
- Edward.
- Robin.

375
00:32:36,921 --> 00:32:39,355
- You escaped.
- I heard England needed saving.

376
00:32:39,424 --> 00:32:41,517
- I have the pact.
- Come on. Come on.

377
00:32:42,593 --> 00:32:44,288
This way.

378
00:32:44,362 --> 00:32:46,922
Hood's in the castle! Seal all exits.

379
00:32:49,567 --> 00:32:51,797
Much?

380
00:32:51,869 --> 00:32:53,393
Well met, my friends.

381
00:32:53,471 --> 00:32:55,439
A new member of the gang.

382
00:33:04,615 --> 00:33:06,515
Yes. The portcullis is open.

383
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:12,354
All soldiers assemble at the main gate.

384
00:33:12,423 --> 00:33:14,186
Going into emergency lockdown.

385
00:33:14,258 --> 00:33:16,123
- So what do we do?
- Keep going.

386
00:33:16,194 --> 00:33:19,493
- No one goes in or out of the castle.
- Halt.

387
00:33:24,469 --> 00:33:27,233
Lads. Let us through.

388
00:33:27,338 --> 00:33:30,102
Nobody leaves. We're going into lockdown.

389
00:33:31,209 --> 00:33:34,906
We're escorting the prisoner
to the Earl of Durham.

390
00:33:44,622 --> 00:33:46,749
Thank you.

391
00:33:46,824 --> 00:33:48,724
Stop him! Stop him!

392
00:33:50,128 --> 00:33:51,823
Nice try.

393
00:33:51,929 --> 00:33:54,625
- Sorry to rain on your parade, Hood.
- That's all right.

394
00:33:55,566 --> 00:33:57,796
Every cloud...

395
00:34:06,944 --> 00:34:08,912
has a silver lining.

396
00:34:08,980 --> 00:34:10,709
Ah!

397
00:34:10,782 --> 00:34:13,478
- Payday, boys!
- Come on, let's go!

398
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:19,922
Everybody. Guards. Get off my money!

399
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:23,091
Split up! You know where to meet.

400
00:34:23,161 --> 00:34:24,822
And ditch those uniforms.

401
00:34:24,929 --> 00:34:26,590
Off!

402
00:34:29,634 --> 00:34:31,602
He's getting away!

403
00:34:45,683 --> 00:34:49,210
Is everyone all right?

404
00:34:51,355 --> 00:34:53,220
Good.

405
00:34:53,324 --> 00:34:56,225
- And where do you think you're going?
- Birkley.

406
00:34:58,796 --> 00:35:01,594
That girl stays here.
She belongs to the Earl of Durham.

407
00:35:01,666 --> 00:35:03,566
No. She belongs with me.

408
00:35:05,803 --> 00:35:08,931
Hand her over or say goodbye to your friend.

409
00:35:09,006 --> 00:35:11,167
Don't listen to him.

410
00:35:11,242 --> 00:35:13,142
Robin, go!

411
00:35:14,145 --> 00:35:16,807
Your mistake, old man, I will kill you.

412
00:35:16,881 --> 00:35:19,145
Leave it, Birkley!

413
00:35:19,217 --> 00:35:22,482
- You're a man of God. You cannot kill.
- Search the square.

414
00:35:22,553 --> 00:35:25,750
And you, Hood, are a man of war
who cannot kill.

415
00:35:30,128 --> 00:35:31,891
Try me.

416
00:35:39,737 --> 00:35:42,103
Edward! No! Get him down.

417
00:35:43,007 --> 00:35:45,100
Here. Here. Djaq?

418
00:35:47,378 --> 00:35:49,846
Don't remove the knife.
I'll prepare my instruments.

419
00:35:49,947 --> 00:35:52,347
John, get John and Beatrice to safety. Now.

420
00:35:52,416 --> 00:35:54,316
This way. Go!

421
00:35:56,053 --> 00:35:58,419
- Leave me.
- I will not, sir.

422
00:35:58,523 --> 00:36:00,150
I will slow you down.

423
00:36:00,224 --> 00:36:02,590
- Go. Go.
- OK.

424
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:13,497
I've never quite understood
my daughter's feelings for you.

425
00:36:13,571 --> 00:36:16,199
Well, I probably don't deserve them.

426
00:36:16,274 --> 00:36:19,732
No. I think maybe you do.

427
00:36:24,448 --> 00:36:26,712
You'd better take this...

428
00:36:26,784 --> 00:36:28,411
pact.

429
00:36:29,120 --> 00:36:31,179
You will not give up your life for mine.

430
00:36:31,255 --> 00:36:32,916
For England.

431
00:36:35,226 --> 00:36:37,160
Robin, listen to me.

432
00:36:39,197 --> 00:36:41,893
For Marian to lose both of us would kill her.

433
00:36:41,966 --> 00:36:44,491
Edward. Edward, that is not going to happen.

434
00:36:45,236 --> 00:36:47,636
Give her a message from me.

435
00:36:47,738 --> 00:36:49,433
Tell...

436
00:36:49,540 --> 00:36:51,337
Tell her...

437
00:36:52,610 --> 00:36:54,635
it's good to dream.

438
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:56,976
I will.

439
00:37:17,201 --> 00:37:19,192
Who's there?

440
00:37:34,418 --> 00:37:36,409
Edward.

441
00:37:40,324 --> 00:37:42,087
Marian.

442
00:37:44,428 --> 00:37:46,191
Guards!

443
00:38:01,145 --> 00:38:03,340
Father.

444
00:38:03,414 --> 00:38:05,382
Father?

445
00:38:06,751 --> 00:38:10,414
Father, wake up. Wake up! Please wake...

446
00:38:12,156 --> 00:38:13,987
Father. Father.

447
00:38:17,328 --> 00:38:19,319
What happened?

448
00:38:19,397 --> 00:38:21,194
What happened? Tell me what happened.

449
00:38:21,265 --> 00:38:23,495
- There were no witnesses, Marian.
- Tell me!

450
00:38:23,567 --> 00:38:27,230
- The Sheriff thinks that he was helping Hood.
- No! He wasn't.

451
00:38:27,338 --> 00:38:29,306
No. No.

452
00:38:36,547 --> 00:38:38,515
I'm sorry.

453
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:41,812
- Marian.
- I'm so sorry.

454
00:38:41,886 --> 00:38:44,218
Father, I'm sorry.

455
00:38:48,359 --> 00:38:50,725
- Marian.
- Can you just...

456
00:38:50,795 --> 00:38:52,490
leave me alone.

457
00:39:01,772 --> 00:39:04,240
- Marian, come away.
- Don't you touch me!

458
00:39:04,975 --> 00:39:06,943
Don't touch me!

459
00:39:11,782 --> 00:39:14,376
Wait. Listen to me.

460
00:39:16,253 --> 00:39:18,949
- This place may not be safe for you now.
- Why?

461
00:39:21,058 --> 00:39:24,289
This is yours, I believe.
Your father's jailer was killed with it.

462
00:39:24,362 --> 00:39:26,353
- I don't care.
- The Sheriff will care.

463
00:39:28,399 --> 00:39:31,835
And when he finds out that it was
your dagger that killed his jailer,

464
00:39:31,936 --> 00:39:33,767
he will hang you.

465
00:39:38,342 --> 00:39:40,207
Let me look after you.

466
00:39:42,980 --> 00:39:44,743
Protect you.

467
00:39:46,016 --> 00:39:47,745
I've always cared about you, Marian.

468
00:39:51,655 --> 00:39:53,589
My feelings for you,

469
00:39:55,192 --> 00:39:57,160
I thought they'd gone away.

470
00:39:58,162 --> 00:40:00,562
But they haven't.

471
00:40:01,198 --> 00:40:03,530
They're stronger than ever.

472
00:40:10,608 --> 00:40:12,838
No.

473
00:40:12,943 --> 00:40:16,140
Forgive me. That was inappropriate.

474
00:40:18,082 --> 00:40:20,550
But in time...

475
00:40:32,730 --> 00:40:35,426
I was with him when he died.

476
00:40:38,569 --> 00:40:40,332
I'm sorry.

477
00:40:45,242 --> 00:40:47,107
Sh.

478
00:40:57,855 --> 00:41:01,313
It's my fault. I told him he was weak.

479
00:41:02,359 --> 00:41:04,327
He died a hero's death.

480
00:41:05,563 --> 00:41:07,895
He got the pact. For England.

481
00:41:07,965 --> 00:41:11,594
- He died believing he had a willful daughter.
- No.

482
00:41:14,738 --> 00:41:16,763
He asked me to give you a message.

483
00:41:18,275 --> 00:41:20,243
"It's good to dream. "

484
00:41:29,854 --> 00:41:31,913
Come with me to the forest.

485
00:41:34,725 --> 00:41:36,693
I've a horse waiting.

486
00:41:40,397 --> 00:41:42,092
Come on.

487
00:42:21,605 --> 00:42:23,732
Do you, John of York,

488
00:42:23,807 --> 00:42:26,970
promise to protect and honor this woman
as long as you both shall live?

489
00:42:27,044 --> 00:42:28,636
I do.

490
00:42:28,746 --> 00:42:32,944
Then I, as the rightful Lord of Locksley
in the county of Nottingham,

491
00:42:33,017 --> 00:42:35,611
now pronounce you man and wife.

492
00:42:36,420 --> 00:42:37,910
You may kiss the bride.

493
00:42:53,070 --> 00:42:54,662
Thank you.

494
00:42:57,207 --> 00:42:59,072
Toasting fork.

495
00:42:59,143 --> 00:43:00,974
Thank you.

496
00:43:07,785 --> 00:43:09,548
Good luck!

497
00:43:10,220 --> 00:43:12,586
You did disarm the trap, didn't you, Will?

